WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.850
Microsoft isn't retiring Active Directory.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.150
It still supports and
develops Windows Server AD.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.987
But every road now points to the
cloud, and the dates are real.

4
00:00:09.987 --> 00:00:15.391
In June 2024 Microsoft
deprecated all versions of NTLM,

5
00:00:15.391 --> 00:00:21.851
and NTLMv1 is removed from Windows
11 24H2 and Windows Server 2025.

6
00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:25.582
On July 1, 2026, Entra ID
began blocking sync from

7
00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:30.175
taking over privileged or
already-mapped cloud accounts.

8
00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:34.176
This month's security update
restricts NTLMv1-derived single

9
00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:38.562
sign-on credentials by default on
devices without Credential Guard.

10
00:00:38.562 --> 00:00:44.515
And by April 7, 2027, every Connect
Sync server must run version 2.6.84.0

11
00:00:44.515 --> 00:00:51.212
or later with application-based
authentication, or synchronization stops.

12
00:00:51.212 --> 00:00:55.792
Behind those dates is a direction:
Cloud Sync replacing Connect Sync,

13
00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:58.363
cloud authentication instead of AD FS,

14
00:00:58.363 --> 00:01:02.862
and sources of authority converted
to the cloud one object at a time.

15
00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.924
The trap is the lift and shift.

16
00:01:04.924 --> 00:01:10.265
Synchronize the forest as it stands, and
twenty-five years of organizational units,

17
00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:14.212
stale accounts and undocumented
trusts arrive in the tenant.

18
00:01:14.212 --> 00:01:17.869
Meanwhile the governance
that the hierarchy carried,

19
00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:22.013
who could manage what and where
policy applied, is left behind,

20
00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:26.300
because Entra ID has no organizational
unit (OU) tree to carry it.
